    "short_description": "Saudi Aramco, officially known as the Saudi Arabian Oil Company, is the largest integrated energy and chemicals company in the world. Headquartered in Dhahran, Saudi Arabia, it is majority state-owned and publicly traded on the Saudi Tadawul stock exchange. With over 76,000 employees, Aramco ranks as the fourth-largest company globally by revenue and is recognized for its significant hydrocarbon reserves, managing more than 270 billion barrels of crude oil.\n\nThe company operates through two main segments: upstream and downstream. Its upstream activities include the exploration and production of oil and natural gas, while the downstream segment focuses on refining, distribution, and marketing of petroleum products, including gasoline and diesel. Aramco serves a diverse customer base across the energy, transportation, and petrochemical industries, with key markets in the United States, India, and China. The company plays a vital role in global oil markets and contributes to Saudi Arabia's economic diversification efforts under Vision 2030.",
